Subject: [PATCH 13/13] fs: wire in the exFAT driver

The two lines that make fs/ build exFAT. The driver itself is not in this
patch: tools/setup-kernel.sh fetches it into fs/exfat at a pinned commit
before the patches are applied, as it does for prima.

exFAT is the factory format of every SD card over 32 GB. Stock read it with
Tuxera's closed texfat.ko, which will not load on a kernel we build, and
Linux only gained its own driver in 5.4 (staging) and 5.7 (fs/exfat), too
far from 3.10 to backport. This is exfat-nofuse 1.2.9, the GPLv2 driver
Samsung published in its Android kernel sources, ported out of them: it
registers as "exfat", which is the name LineageOS' vold mounts and looks
for in /proc/filesystems, and it takes vold's uid/gid/fmask/dmask options.
The userspace half, fsck.exfat and mkfs.exfat, LineageOS already ships.
---
diff --git fs/Kconfig fs/Kconfig
--- fs/Kconfig
+++ fs/Kconfig
@@ -92,6 +92,7 @@
 menu "DOS/FAT/NT Filesystems"
 
 source "fs/fat/Kconfig"
+source "fs/exfat/Kconfig"
 source "fs/ntfs/Kconfig"
 
 endmenu
diff --git fs/Makefile fs/Makefile
--- fs/Makefile
+++ fs/Makefile
@@ -77,6 +77,7 @@
 obj-$(CONFIG_CODA_FS)		+= coda/
 obj-$(CONFIG_MINIX_FS)		+= minix/
 obj-$(CONFIG_FAT_FS)		+= fat/
+obj-$(CONFIG_EXFAT_FS)		+= exfat/
 obj-$(CONFIG_BFS_FS)		+= bfs/
 obj-$(CONFIG_ISO9660_FS)	+= isofs/
 obj-$(CONFIG_HFSPLUS_FS)	+= hfsplus/ # Before hfs to find wrapped HFS+
